*#News Browser*

A simple Android app that fetches the New York Times Top Stories and displays them in a scrollable list with thumbnails. Tapping an article opens a detail screen with the abstract and a link to the full story. Built for students learning Android with Kotlin.

Table of Contents
Installation
Usage
Contributing
License

**Installation**
Clone or download the project and open it in Android Studio.
Add the dependencies from build-gradle-additions.txt to your Gradle files (AsyncHttpClient, kotlinx-serialization, Glide, RecyclerView) and apply the serialization plugin.
Copy the entries from AndroidManifest-additions.xml into your AndroidManifest.xml (internet permission and DetailActivity).
Get a free API key from developer.nytimes.com with the Top Stories API enabled.
In MainActivity.kt, replace YOUR_NYT_API_KEY with your key.
Sync Gradle and run the app on an emulator or device.

**Usage**
Launch the app to load the latest Top Stories into a RecyclerView.
Scroll through the articles, each showing a thumbnail, title, and byline.
Tap an article to open the detail screen, then use the button to read the full story in your browser.

